# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Primitives {#primitives}"
msgstr "Primitives {#primitives}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All physical systems, whether classical or quantum, can exist in different "
"states. For example, a car on a road can have a certain mass, position, "
"speed, or acceleration that characterize its state. Similarly, quantum "
"systems can also have different configurations or states, but they differ "
"from classical systems in how we deal with measurements and state evolution."
" This leads to unique properties such as *superposition* and *entanglement* "
"that are exclusive to quantum mechanics. Just like we can describe a car's "
"state using physical properties like speed or acceleration, we can also "
"describe the state of a quantum system using *observables*, which are "
"mathematical objects.\n"
msgstr ""
"古典・量子を問わず、あらゆる物理系はさまざまな状態を取り得ます。たとえば、道路上の車は質量・位置・速度・加速度といった物理量によってその状態が特徴付けられます。同様に、量子系も異なる配置や状態を持ちますが、測定や状態の時間発展の扱い方が古典系とは異なります。これにより、量子力学に固有の*重ね合わせ*や*エンタングルメント*といった特性が生じます。車の状態を速度や加速度などの物理量で記述できるように、量子系の状態も数学的オブジェクトである*オブザーバブル*を用いて記述できます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In quantum mechanics, states are represented by normalized complex column "
"vectors, or *kets* ($|\\psi\\rangle$), and observables are Hermitian linear "
"operators ($\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$) that act on the kets. An "
"eigenvector ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) of an observable is known as an "
"*eigenstate*. Measuring an observable for one of its eigenstates "
"($|\\lambda\\rangle$) will give us the corresponding eigenvalue ($\\lambda$)"
" as readout.\n"
msgstr ""
"量子力学では、状態は規格化された複素数の列ベクトル、すなわち*ケット*（$|\\psi\\rangle$）で表され、オブザーバブルはケットに作用するエルミート線形演算子（$\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$）で表されます。オブザーバブルの固有ベクトル（$|\\lambda\\rangle$）は*固有状態*と呼ばれます。オブザーバブルをその固有状態のひとつ（$|\\lambda\\rangle$）に対して測定すると、対応する固有値（$\\lambda$）が読み出しとして得られます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you're wondering how to measure a quantum system and what you can "
"measure, Qiskit offers two <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Basic and "
"fundamental operations or data type. Qiskit has the Sampler and Estimator "
"primitives to serve as building blocks to easily construct complex "
"algorithmic workloads.\">primitives</DefinitionTooltip> that can help:\n"
msgstr ""
"量子系をどのように測定するか、そして何を測定できるかについては、Qiskit が提供する 2 つの <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"基本的かつ根本的な演算またはデータ型。Qiskit "
"には、複雑なアルゴリズムのワークロードを簡単に構築するためのビルディングブロックとして、Sampler と Estimator の primitive "
"があります。\">primitive</DefinitionTooltip> が役立ちます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Sampler`: Given a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive obtains "
"the probability of each possible computational basis state.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Sampler`：量子状態 $|\\psi\\rangle$ が与えられた場合、この primitive "
"は各計算基底状態が得られる確率を求めます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Estimator`: Given a quantum observable $\\hat{H}$ and a state "
"$|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive computes the expected value of "
"$\\hat{H}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Estimator`：量子オブザーバブル $\\hat{H}$ と状態 $|\\psi\\rangle$ が与えられた場合、この primitive "
"は $\\hat{H}$ の期待値を計算します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Sampler primitive {#the-sampler-primitive}"
msgstr "Sampler primitive {#the-sampler-primitive}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Sampler` primitive calculates the probability of obtaining each "
"possible state $|k\\rangle$ from the computational basis, given a quantum "
"circuit that prepares the state $|\\psi\\rangle$. It calculates\n"
msgstr ""
"`Sampler` primitive は、状態 $|\\psi\\rangle$ を準備する量子 Circuit が与えられたとき、計算基底の各状態 "
"$|k\\rangle$ が得られる確率を計算します。具体的には以下を計算します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Where $n$ is the number of qubits, and $k$ the integer representation of any"
" possible output binary string $\\{0,1\\}^n$ (that is, integers base $2$).\n"
msgstr "ここで $n$ は qubit の数、$k$ は任意の出力バイナリ文字列 $\\{0,1\\}^n$ の整数表現（すなわち 2 進数の整数）です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit Runtime [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/sampler-v2) runs the circuit multiple times on a quantum device, "
"performing measurements on each run, and reconstructing the probability "
"distribution from the recovered bitstrings. The more runs (or *shots*) it "
"performs, the more accurate the results will be, but this requires more time"
" and quantum resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit Runtime の [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/sampler-v2) は、量子デバイス上で Circuit "
"を複数回実行し、各実行で測定を行い、得られたビット列から確率分布を復元します。実行回数（*ショット数*）が多いほど結果は正確になりますが、より多くの時間と量子リソースが必要です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, since the number of possible outputs grows exponentially with the "
"number of qubits $n$ (that is, $2^n$), the number of shots will need to grow"
" exponentially as well in order to capture a _dense_ probability "
"distribution. Therefore, `Sampler` is only efficient for *sparse* "
"probability distributions; where the target state $|\\psi\\rangle$ must be "
"expressible as a linear combination of the computational basis states, with "
"the number of terms growing at most polynomially with the number of "
"qubits:\n"
msgstr ""
"ただし、可能な出力の数は qubit 数 $n$ に対して指数的に増加する（すなわち "
"$2^n$）ため、*密な*確率分布を捉えるにはショット数も指数的に増やす必要があります。そのため、`Sampler` "
"が効率的に機能するのは*疎な*確率分布の場合に限られます。ここで、目標状態 $|\\psi\\rangle$ "
"は計算基底状態の線形結合として表現可能であり、その項数が qubit 数に対して高々多項式的に増加することが条件です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Sampler` can also be configured to retrieve probabilities from a "
"subsection of the circuit, representing a subset of the total possible "
"states.\n"
msgstr "また `Sampler` は、Circuit の一部分（全状態の部分集合）から確率を取得するように設定することもできます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Estimator primitive {#the-estimator-primitive}"
msgstr "Estimator primitive {#the-estimator-primitive}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Estimator` primitive calculates the expectation value of an observable "
"$\\hat{H}$ for a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$; where the observable "
"probabilities can be expressed as $p_\\lambda = "
"|\\langle\\lambda|\\psi\\rangle|^2$, being $|\\lambda\\rangle$ the "
"eigenstates of the observable $\\hat{H}$. The expectation value is then "
"defined as the average of all possible outcomes $\\lambda$ (that is, the "
"eigenvalues of the observable) of a measurement of the state "
"$|\\psi\\rangle$, weighted by the corresponding probabilities:\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"しかし、オブザーバブルの期待値を計算することは常に可能とは限りません。固有基底が未知の場合が多いからです。Qiskit Runtime の "
"[`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/estimator-v2) "
"は、複雑な代数的処理を用いて、実際の量子デバイス上でオブザーバブルを固有基底が既知の他のオブザーバブルの組み合わせに分解することで期待値を推定します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English:
# 簡単に言えば、`Estimator` は測定方法が不明なオブザーバブルを、<DefinitionTooltip defi
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, calculating the expectation value of an observable is not always "
"possible, as we often don't know its eigenbasis. The Qiskit Runtime "
"[`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/estimator-v2) uses a complex algebraic process to estimate the "
"expectation value on a real quantum device by breaking down the observable "
"into a combination of other observables whose eigenbasis we do know.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: $$ \hat{P}_k :=
# \sigma_{k_{n-1}}\otimes \cdots \otimes \sigm
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simpler terms, `Estimator` breaks down any observable that it doesn't know how to measure into simpler, measurable observables called <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set of matrices commonly used in quantum computing to represent and manipulate quantum states, consisting of the identity matrix and the three Pauli matrices (X, Y, and Z).\">Pauli operators</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
"Any operator can be expressed as a combination of $4^n$ Pauli operators.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{P}_k :=\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} \\quad\n"
"\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,4^n-1\\}, \\\\\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr "このとき\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "such that\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"ここで $n$ は qubit 数、$k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$（$k_l \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 "
"\\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$、すなわち 4 進数の整数）、$(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, "
"\\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$ です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $n$ is the number of qubits, $k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$ for $k_l "
"\\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 \\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ (that is, integers base $4$), "
"and $(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, \\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"この分解を行った後、`Estimator` は元の Circuit から各オブザーバブル $\\hat{P}_k$ に対して新しい Circuit "
"$V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ を導出し、パウリオブザーバブルを計算基底で効果的に*対角化*して測定します。パウリオブザーバブルは $V_k$ "
"が事前に分かっているため容易に測定できますが、一般のオブザーバブルではそうではありません。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After performing this decomposition, `Estimator` derives a new circuit "
"$V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ for each observable $\\hat{P}_k$ (from the original "
"circuit), to effectively *diagonalize* the Pauli observable in the "
"computational basis and measure it. We can easily measure Pauli observables "
"because we know $V_k$ ahead of time, which is not the case generally for "
"other observables.\n"
msgstr ""
"各 $\\hat{P}_{k}$ について、`Estimator` は対応する Circuit "
"を量子デバイス上で複数回実行し、計算基底で出力状態を測定し、各可能な出力 $j$ が得られる確率 $p_{kj}$ を計算します。次に各出力 $j$ "
"に対応する $P_k$ の固有値 $\\lambda_{kj}$ を求め、$w_k$ と掛け合わせ、全ての結果を足し合わせて状態 "
"$|\\psi\\rangle$ に対するオブザーバブル $\\hat{H}$ の期待値を得ます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each $\\hat{P}_{k}$, the `Estimator` runs the corresponding circuit on a"
" quantum device multiple times, measures the output state in the "
"computational basis, and calculates the probability $p_{kj}$ of obtaining "
"each possible output $j$. It then looks for the eigenvalue $\\lambda_{kj}$ "
"of $P_k$ corresponding to each output $j$, multiplies by $w_k$, and adds all"
" the results together to obtain the expected value of the observable "
"$\\hat{H}$ for the given state $|\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"
"Since calculating the expectation value of $4^n$ Paulis is impractical (that is, exponentially growing), `Estimator` can only be efficient when a large amount of $w_k$ are zero (that is, *sparse* Pauli decomposition instead of *dense*). Formally we say that, for this computation to be *efficiently solvable*, the number of non-zero terms has to grow at most polynomially with the number of qubits $n$: $\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k \\hat{P}_k.$\n"
msgstr ""
"$4^n$ 個のパウリの期待値を計算することは（指数的に増加するため）非現実的であり、`Estimator` が効率的に機能するのは $w_k$ "
"の大部分がゼロの場合（すなわち*密な*分解ではなく*疎な*パウリ分解）に限られます。形式的には、この計算が*効率的に解ける*ためには、非ゼロ項の数が "
"qubit 数 $n$ に対して高々多項式的に増加することが必要です：$\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k"
" \\hat{P}_k.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The reader may notice the implicit assumption that probability "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The process of taking several measurements "
"of one or several things.\">sampling</DefinitionTooltip> also needs to be "
"efficient as explained for `Sampler`, which means\n"
msgstr ""
"`Sampler` で説明したように、確率の<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"1 "
"つまたは複数の事象を複数回測定するプロセス。\">サンプリング</DefinitionTooltip>も効率的である必要があるという暗黙の仮定があることに読者は気づくでしょう。すなわち\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Guided example to calculate expectation values {#guided-example-to-"
"calculate-expectation-values}"
msgstr "期待値計算のガイド付き例 {#guided-example-to-calculate-expectation-values}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's assume the single-qubit state $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = "
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$, and observable\n"
msgstr ""
"単一 qubit の状態 $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + "
"|1\\rangle)$ と、以下のオブザーバブルを考えます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"with the following theoretical expectation value $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+"
" = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2.$\n"
msgstr "理論的な期待値は $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2$ です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since we do not know how to measure this observable, we cannot compute its "
"expectation value directly, and we need to re-express it as "
"$\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = 2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+"
" $. Which can be shown to evaluate to the same result by virtue of noting "
"that $\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$, and $\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"このオブザーバブルを直接測定する方法が分からないため、期待値を直接計算することはできず、$\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = "
"2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+$ "
"として再表現する必要があります。$\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$、$\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$ "
"であることから、同じ結果が得られることが確認できます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let see how to compute $\\langle X \\rangle_+$ and $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$ "
"directly. Since $X$ and $Z$ do not commute (that is, they don't share the "
"same eigenbasis), they cannot be measured simultaneously, therefore we need "
"the auxiliary circuits:\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\langle X \\rangle_+$ と $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$ を直接計算する方法を見てみましょう。$X$ と "
"$Z$ は可換でない（すなわち、固有基底が共有されていない）ため、同時に測定することはできません。そのため、補助 Circuit が必要です。\n"

